[h1]MaoLib - L4D2 VScript Framework[/h1]
[i]Version 2.2 | Standalone VScript library for Left 4 Dead 2.[/i]
[b]Zero external dependencies. Not VSLib. Not Lua. Pure Squirrel 3.0 on the native Source API.[/b]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]What is MaoLib?[/h2]
A modular VScript framework for L4D2. Originally the backbone of Lost 4 Creed (16 addons, 3300+ lines of gameplay), now a standalone library.

[b]10 subsystems:[/b]
[list]
[*] Centralized timer manager (single logic_timer, no AddThinkToEnt)
[*] NavMesh pathfinding: high ground, choke points, flanking, LOS, flow distance
[*] AoE system with selector/applicator pipeline
[*] Visual effects: particles, explosions, impacts, screenshake
[*] HUD messaging with throttle, queue, color presets
[*] Per-player state registry (auto-cleanup)
[*] Movement modifiers: speed/friction stacking with auto-expiry
[*] Status Effects v3.0: DoT + flat key-value registry
[*] Map utilities: spawning, director helpers, entity finders
[*] Timer monitoring and leak detection
[/list]

All code is native VScript - no wrappers, no DLLs.

[hr][/hr]

[h2]MaoLib vs. Other Libraries[/h2]

[h3]vs. HeavyUtils (predecessor)[/h3]
HeavyUtils is the single-file utility (~50 functions) that inspired MaoLib's core loop. MaoLib extends far beyond:

[table]
[tr][th]Feature[/th][th]HeavyUtils[/th][th]MaoLib[/th][/tr]
[tr][td]Architecture[/td][td]Monolithic[/td][td]11 modular files[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Timer system[/td][td]None[/td][td]Full centralized manager with stats[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]NavMesh tools[/td][td]None[/td][td]High ground, chokes, flanking, flow distance[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Area of Effect[/td][td]None[/td][td]4 selectors + 8 applicators[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]HUD system[/td][td]None[/td][td]4 channels with throttle and colors[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Player state[/td][td]None[/td][td]Key-value per UID, auto-cleanup[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Modifiers[/td][td]None[/td][td]Speed/friction stacking, multi-source[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Status/DoT[/td][td]None[/td][td]DoT subsystem + flat registry[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]VFX[/td][td]None[/td][td]Budget-based priority, safe spawning[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Config parser[/td][td]Raw compilestring (unsafe)[/td][td]Allowlist-validated, injection-safe[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Documentation[/td][td]Minimal comments[/td][td]Full API per module + README[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[b]vs. VSLib[/b]
[table]
[tr][th]Aspect[/th][th]VSLib[/th][th]MaoLib[/th][/tr]
[tr][td]Philosophy[/td][td]OOP wrappers over entities[/td][td]Direct native calls + helpers[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Timer management[/td][td]None[/td][td]Full centralized system[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Runtime state[/td][td]Maintains entity table[/td][td]Stateless (except timers)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Performance[/td][td]Wrapper overhead[/td][td]Zero overhead[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Debugging[/td][td]Stack through wrappers[/td][td]Direct to modder's code[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[i]Note:[/i] VSLib's repository is used in Lost 4 Creed only as a method-verification reference. [b]MaoLib does not use VSLib at runtime.[/b] Both can coexist.

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Module Architecture[/h2]
[code]director_base_addon.nut     <- Entry point (auto-loads all)
+-- maolib.nut           <- Core: timers, iterators, math, config
    +-- maolib_timers_cleanup  <- Monitoring + leak detection
    +-- maolib_vfx.nut         <- Particles, explosions, screenshake
    +-- maolib_navutils.nut    <- NavMesh: LOS, high ground, chokes
+-- maolib_state.nut     <- PlayerState per UID
+-- maolib_hud.nut       <- Chat, center, hint, game_text
+-- maolib_modifiers.nut <- Speed/friction stacking
+-- maolib_aoe.nut       <- Selectors + applicators
+-- maolib_status.nut    <- DoT + flat registry
+-- maolib_mapper.nut    <- Map utilities[/code]

Each module is independent. Include what you need.

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Technical Highlights[/h2]

[h3]Timer Manager[/h3]
[code]MaoLib.AddTimer("name", interval, callback)    // Recurrent
MaoLib.DelayCall(callback, delay)               // One-shot
MaoLib.RemoveTimer() / PauseTimer() / ResumeTimer()
MaoLib.ClearAllTimers()                          // On round_end[/code]
Single logic_timer (immune to AddThinkToEnt). All callbacks in ::MaoLib.Timers{}. Method detachment protection via closure wrapper. Per-timer stats. 100 Hz max resolution.

[h3]Damage Recursion Guard (MANDATORY)[/h3]
TakeDamage() inside player_hurt/infected_hurt triggers another event. Without a guard: infinite recursion.
[code]_processingDamageEvent = false
function OnGameEvent_player_hurt(params) {
    if (_processingDamageEvent) return
    _processingDamageEvent = true
    // ... TakeDamage() ...
    _processingDamageEvent = false
}[/code]
Use a single flag for both events to prevent cross-event ping-pong (player_hurt -> AoE hits infected -> infected_hurt -> and back).

[h3]Secure Config Parser[/h3]
Unlike raw compilestring(), MaoLib validates input against a character allowlist before parsing. Control characters (\\n, \\r, \\t) are rejected, preventing injection via untrusted input.

[h3]AoE Architecture (Select -> Apply)[/h3]
[code]// Phase 1: Select targets
local targets = MaoLib.AoE.Select.Circle(origin, 500, {
    className = "infected", aliveOnly = true, requireLOS = true
})
// Phase 2: Apply effect
MaoLib.AoE.Apply.Damage(targets, 100, attacker, DMG_BULLET, {
    falloff = "linear", origin = origin, radius = 500, minDamage = 10
})[/code]
[b]Selectors:[/b] Circle, Cone, Line, ExpandingCircle (shockwave).
[b]Applicators:[/b] Damage, Heal, HealTemp, Stagger, Push, ModifierSpeed, ModifierFriction, Callback.

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]Versions:[/b] All L4D2 builds (VScript unchanged since 2012)
[*] [b]Modes:[/b] All - Coop, Versus, Survival, Scavenge, Realism, Mutation, Campaign
[*] [b]VSLib/HeavyUtils:[/b] Compatible, can coexist
[*] [b]SourceMod:[/b] Compatible - different layer (.smx plugins)
[*] [b]Other mods:[/b] Only adds ::MaoLib and ::MaoLib_VFX to root table
[/list]

[b]Known engine limitations (documented in README):[/b]
[list]
[*] info_particle_system needs effect_name at spawn - post-spawn __KeyValueFromString fails
[*] ambient_generic.SetParent() unsupported - use SourceEntityName on info_target
[*] LookupBone on "infected" CRASHES - use GetEffectPosition()
[*] light_dynamic.SetOrigin() while on does not update visually - toggle TurnOff/On
[*] ApplyAbsVelocityImpulse blocked on players - use Stagger() or NetProps
[/list]

